    "summary": "The router keeps a per-thread in-flight map and publishes ThreadStatus (role, cls, session, busy, oldest method/since, FIFO queued) on attach, send, end (reply, terminal frame, lifetime completion, cancel of a stream without a lifetime) and FIFO changes; detach forgets the thread and publishes nothing for an unattached thread. Deviation from the LLD's roleOf option: role, class and session are read from the target registry the router already holds (registry.targets()), so no roleOf option is needed. Wired in index.ts with threadServices.board.",
